        "original_id": "91e98d16-faec-5d64-b0f2-a92922bd6247",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Valie Export, Gary Sherman, Melody Anderson, Jack Albertson, James Farentino\n- Works: The Practice of Love, Dead & Buried, Death Line, Poltergeist III\n- Topics: contemporary arts, horror film genre\n\nFacts:\n- Gary Sherman was born in 1945 and is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer from Chicago, Illinois.\n- Dead & Buried is a 1981 science fiction horror film directed by Gary Sherman and starring Melody Anderson, Jack Albertson, and James Farentino.\n- The Practice of Love is a 1985 Austrian drama film written and directed by Valie Export.\n- Gary Sherman is best known for prolific work in the horror film genre, including directing Death Line, Dead & Buried, and Poltergeist III.\n- Valie Export's artistic work includes video installations, body performances, expanded cinema, computer animations, photography, sculptures, and publications covering contemporary arts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
